   "unmapped": [
    "Principal-agent game: principal offers incentive vector, agent picks arm maximizing her empirical mean plus incentive; principal observes chosen arm and own reward but not agent's reward",
    "Regret benchmark uses per-round optimal incentive depending on agent's empirical means"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "At each round t, the agent selects an arm A_t that maximizes the empirical mean plus an incentive proposed by the principal: A_t \\in \\argmax_{a} {\\hatmu_a(t)+\\pi_a(t)} ... the reward of each arm a for the principal is drawn from a [0,1]-bounded distribution D^P_a with mean \\theta_a, and the reward of each arm a for the agent is drawn from another [0,1]-bounded distribution D^A_a with mean \\mu_a."
  },
